<p>An explosion at Huasheng Fireworks Manufacturing and Display Company in Liuyang, Hunan province, killed at least 26 people and injured 61 others, state media and local authorities reported Tuesday. The blast struck Monday afternoon in Liuyang, a county-level city administered by Changsha, and officials had not announced a cause.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/HJGB-_fQZKIo8ic-xI8HABFhfDW8OF4SaKEhLVhM4p1JpKUJ7okNyVL7ZtvLRnZVfohcwZgRQ5VE0MKzSiykiv-OXp1K_lJzb0R8QLEYfOd-gSbEjOzW2BPmhKrr-bSF9dxy_9Y5a0wNbOY1Qr0Kun5nWVOvMBqnJR4f26C32pKWYuQ2C271QeiYqTNAGw4Hn1uA4_PeLk6AZk2efVYc0Kx-z4BSJY3WtqYIX_li2ARnAd76zYAOYbJpm_r8fuksdXKMpCaY8eGtbPUVUg' alt='Firefighters work to extinguish a fire following a blast at a fireworks manufacturing factory in Liuyang, Hunan province, China, May 5, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Rescue scale: More than 480 rescuers, organized into five teams, and three rescue robots were deployed for grid-style searches at the site.</li><li>Safety perimeter: Authorities evacuated residents, set a 1-km rescue area and established a 3-km control zone because two black powder warehouses inside the compound posed secondary risks.</li><li>Site damage: State media footage showed collapsed or damaged facilities, debris and smoke still rising from parts of the plant Tuesday.</li><li>Police action: Police detained the person in charge of the company while investigators examined the cause of the blast.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Xi Jinping: The Chinese president called for a speedy inquiry into the cause, strict accountability and stronger risk screening and hazard controls in key industries. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1997692/blast-at-fireworks-factory-in-chinas-hunan-kills-21-state-media-says'>Xinhua via Dawn</a>)</li><li>Changsha Mayor Chen Bozhang: Chen said search and rescue at the scene was largely complete, but officials were still verifying casualties and identifying victims. (<a href='https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/world/2